{
  "manufacturer": "Vaisala",
  "manufacturer_slug": "vaisala",
  "model": "DMP Series dew point probes (DMP5, DMP6, DMP7, DMP8) (Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "dmp-series",
  "short_model": "DMP5-DMP8",
  "aliases": [
    "DMP5",
    "DMP6",
    "DMP7",
    "DMP8",
    "DRYCAP DMP series"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Sensor (dew point probe)",
  "applies_to": "Vaisala DMP5, DMP6, DMP7 and DMP8 dew point and temperature probes, Modbus RTU interface (user guide M212357EN-F).",
  "summary": "The DMP Series are Vaisala DRYCAP dew point and temperature probes for industrial drying, compressed air and high-temperature processes. Each probe is a Modbus RTU slave on RS-485 and also works with Indigo transmitters. This map covers dew/frost point and calculated humidity values, diagnostics, status, compensation, purge, filtering, serial settings and test registers.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 240,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "1-based",
    "note": "The guide numbers registers in decimal starting at 1 and also prints the 0-based hex address used in the request; register number 1 is address 0x0000 on the wire."
  },
  "default_word_order": "CDAB",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "DMP Series User Guide",
    "doc_number": "M212357EN-F",
    "revision_date": "2025-05",
    "url": "https://docs.vaisala.com/r/M212357EN-F/en-US",
    "pages": "Appendix A Modbus reference, pp. 80-90 (Tables 37-49)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "All registers are holding registers: read with function 03, write with function 16.",
    "32-bit floats and 32-bit integers put the least significant word at the listed register (CDAB). The guide states this and its worked read example confirms it.",
    "Unavailable data reads as quiet NaN (float) or 0x8000 (16-bit integer) rather than an exception.",
    "Integer registers use the scale listed per register (raw x 0.01 for most temperature and humidity values).",
    "Register 513 reads 0 when an error is active and 1 when there is none, as printed in the guide.",
    "Left out: device tag text (2561).",
    "Output values are frozen at the last valid reading while sensor purge, autocalibration or condensation prevention runs; register 514 shows this."
  ],
